    <h1>Social Media Ideas</h1><ul><li><p><strong>image generation</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Extract dates from syllabus and inject into google docs</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Research someone on linkedin and provide a summary</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Research all matches at the us open this year and place in a spreadsheet</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>give me a list of the top 20 people who have emailed me this month and place in a spreadsheet</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>research the dates of all patriots games this year and place in my calendar</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>download apple third quarter results pdf and provide a summary in a new google doc</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>inventory tracker, give me an estimated value of each item</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>“That conference agenda PDF where you can’t find the room number for your session.”</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>The “terms and conditions” of your credit card.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Car rental terms &amp; conditions.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Spotify playlist exported to Excel.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Spreadsheet ranking every restaurant in town.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>The 120-page PhD dissertation PDF</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Ski resort trail map PDF.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Car buying comparison spreadsheet</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Subscription cancellation policy PDF.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Personal horoscope report PDF</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Restaurant “to try” spreadsheet.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Making grocery lists from recipes.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Workflow thread</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Tweet 1:</strong> “AI workflows that evolve with your needs? That’s Banbury.”<br><strong>Tweet 2:</strong> “– It reads your Gmail.<br>– It understands natural language.<br>– It schedules your meetings.<br>– It learns and scales over time.”<br><strong>Tweet 3 (CTA):</strong> “Want to streamline your everyday work? Learn more: [link]”</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>“Which would you want Banbury to automate first?</strong><br>A) Read emails, extract action items<br>B) Read PDF’s, write a summary<br>C) Automatically fill out forms on the web</p></li></ul><p><br>Let us know, and watch as AI becomes your team’s silent partner. [link]”</p><ul><li><p><strong>"What if" Scenarios</strong></p><p>"What if your AI could:</p><p>✅ Read your emails and extract action items</p><p>✅ Schedule meetings based on context clues</p><p>✅ Draft responses in your writing style</p><p>✅ Learn your preferences over time</p><p></p><p>Stop imagining. Start using Banbury. [link]"</p></li></ul><p>• <strong>Productivity Hack Series</strong></p><p>"Productivity hack #1: Stop managing your AI, start conversing with it.</p><p>Instead of: 'Create calendar event, title: Team Meeting, date: 2024-01-15'</p><p>Try: 'Set up our weekly team sync starting next Monday'</p><p>• <strong>Quick Win Examples</strong></p><p>"Quick wins with Banbury:</p><p></p><p>📧 'Summarize this email thread' → Instant brief</p><p>📅 'Find time for coffee with John' → Meeting scheduled</p><p>📝 'Draft a follow-up for yesterday's client call' → Email ready</p><p></p><p>Small requests, big time savings. Try it: [link]"</p><p></p>
